#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0100 expect=violation domain=EC
#note "H3 convergence (ruled 2026-08-19) as AMENDED BY PHASE 6c (D117/D95d): the dose leg is the hole-free bare comparison ECDOSE <= 0. The ECOCCUR column is ABSENT (Perm in EC; treat-as-empty applies per D-TA-4c and the guard tolerates it). Row 1 has ECDOSE=0 recorded -> fires; row 2 has ECDOSE > 0 -> silent. ROW 3 LEAVES ECDOSE EMPTY AND NOW FIRES: under D34 #5 every MissingValue sorts BELOW every non-missing value and #5-2 makes the comparison total, so a missing dose IS not-greater-than-0 - which is exactly what this rule's Message asserts. D95d ruled these four ECDOSE <= 0 rules KEEP on that authority: the operand that goes missing is the SUBJECT of the assertion (D96d), so the new firing is a bug fix, not a false positive. The 2026-08-19 note's handover of the missing-dose case to CDISC-CG0462 was written under the pre-flip semantics; CG0462 still reports it under its own aspect (ECDOSTXT empty when ECDOSE is missing), so the row now carries two findings from two rules - ordinary rule overlap, not a defect."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 2
#expectViolationAt row=1 ECSEQ=1 USUBJID=01-701-1015
#expectViolationAt row=3 ECSEQ=3 USUBJID=01-701-1028
dataset EC label="Exposure as Collected"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col ECSEQ type=Num label="Sequence Number"
col ECSTAT type=Char label="Completion Status"
col ECDOSTXT type=Char label="Dose Description"
col ECDOSE type=Num label="Dose per Administration"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | EC | 01-701-1015 | 1 |  |  | 0
CDISCPILOT01 | EC | 01-701-1023 | 2 |  |  | 100
CDISCPILOT01 | EC | 01-701-1028 | 3 |  |  |
